# Source media is user-supplied and large; the tutorial ships samples separately,
# not full clips. Never commit a real end-user video — a reader's or the
# author's own pilot footage may carry rights the author cannot redistribute.
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov

# Narrow, deliberate exception: starter/sample/ is a purpose-built synthetic
# clip (generated background + offline TTS narration, see starter/sample/README.md)
# with no rights ambiguity, committed specifically so a reader can see a real
# result and run the gate chain before installing anything. This does NOT
# reopen the door to committing real footage anywhere else in the repo.
!/starter/sample/*.mp4

# Generated subtitle/caption working files from running the tutorial yourself —
# the repo ships example .srt files under starter/, not your own run's output.
/starter/output/
*.srt.bak

# Per-run evidence, not a repo constant — see starter/versions.lock.template.
# Never commit the filled-in file; only the template is tracked.
/starter/versions.lock

# Scratch preview frames
*_frame_*.png
preview_frame*.png

# dist/ IS tracked — the generated .docx/.pptx are deliverables, same as
# gstack-tutorial-2. Do not add dist/ here.

# Python / build
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
_build/__pycache__/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
